      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:7:30:14",
      "text": [
        " كُلُّ مُسْكِرٍ حَرَامٌ وَ كُلُّ مُخَمَّرٍ حَرَامٌ وَ الْفُقَّاعُ حَرَامٌ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Muhammad Bin Musa, from Muhammad Bin Isa, from Al Hassan Bin Ali Al Washa, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Al-Hassan Al-Reza<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘Every intoxicant is Prohibited, and every brewing is Prohibited, and the fermented drinks are Prohibited’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "14. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Muhammad ibn Musa from Muhammad ibn ‘Isa from al-Hassan ibn Ali al-Washsha’ who has said the following: “Abu al-Hassan, al-Rida’, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘All intoxicating substances are unlawful, everything confusing the power of reason is unlawful and al-Fuqa’ (beer) is unlawful.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
